Apple's chief hardware officer Johny Srouji is being considered as a potential successor to Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang as the chipmaker's board prepares to remove its co-founder, according to <a href="https://www.semafor.com/article/11/11/2026/nvidia-board-preparing-to-oust-ceo-huang-wsj"><em>Semafor</em></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/johny-srouji.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1077078" /><br/>
Citing a person familiar with the matter, the publication identified Srouji as one of the people under consideration for Nvidia's top job. It is unclear if Srouji has yet been approached or expressed interest in leaving Apple.<br/>
<br/>
Nvidia has reportedly hired an outside firm to identify potential replacements for Huang, according to <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-12/nvidia-drama-triggers-difficult-search-for-huang-s-successor"><em>Bloomberg</em></a>. The succession discussions follow reports of multiple extramarital affairs involving Huang, including one with a woman reportedly suspected of spying for China. Some directors apparently favor appointing chief financial officer Colette Kress as interim CEO if Huang is removed.<br/>
<br/>
Srouji's emergence as a possible candidate comes just months after a substantial expansion of his responsibilities at Apple. In April, Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/20/srouji-chief-hardware-officer/">promoted him</a> from senior vice president of hardware technologies to chief hardware officer alongside the announcement that John Ternus would <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/20/tim-cook-stepping-down/">succeed Tim Cook</a> as CEO. Srouji took over the hardware engineering organization previously led by Ternus while retaining oversight of Apple's custom chips and other hardware technologies.<br/>
<br/>
The promotion followed uncertainty about Srouji's future at Apple. In December 2025, <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> reported that Srouji had told Cook he was <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/12/07/SROUJI-COULD-BE-NEXT-TO-GO-AS-EXODUS-CONTINUES/">seriously considering leaving</a> for another company. Cook was reportedly trying to retain him with increased compensation and broader responsibilities. Srouji subsequently <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/12/08/johny-srouji-provides-career-update/">told employees</a> that he did not plan to leave "anytime soon."<br/>
<br/>
Srouji helped lead the Mac's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2022/04/18/apple-silicon-johny-srouji-interview/">transition to Apple silicon</a>, and his hardware technologies organization also oversees areas including cellular modems, cameras, displays, sensors, and batteries. Srouji joined Apple in 2008 to lead development of the A4 chip after holding senior processor development and design roles at Intel and IBM. He was also reportedly <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2019/01/15/johny-srouji-intel-ceo-candidate/">considered for Intel's CEO position</a> in 2019, although that role ultimately <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2019/01/31/intel-names-robert-swan-ceo/">went to Bob Swan</a>.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/johny-srouji/">Johny Srouji</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/nvidia/">Nvidia</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/12/johny-srouji-eyed-as-potential-nvidia-ceo/">Apple&#039;s Johny Srouji Eyed to Replace Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apples-johny-srouji-eyed-to-replace-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang.2494235/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>